nd is willing  to upskill yourself to understand the  nuts and bolts of business functions  than an mba could be a credible option  through this kind of immersive learning  experience you can excel in the company  that you're currently employed at or  even transition towards managerial  positions  let's talk about the structure and  curriculum of an online mba program  as the name suggests the main idea  behind online mba programs is to help  students obtain the degree at their  convenience it is usually designed to  match the on-campus curriculum as  closely as possible the course content  is delivered via online live lectures  recorded sessions and interactive video  conferences some of the top online  programs include career coaching  sessions and placement fairs as well  the durations for these programs are  quite flexible some universities offer  accelerated one-year programs while  others offer extended part-time tracks  spanning up to two to five years  considering that most students enrolled  in the course are working professionals  with heavy job commitments the  flexibility of academic scheduling is by  far the most important component of the  appeal around online mba programs  besides the advantages of pursuing an  mba degree at the time of your choice  and from the comfort of the couch there  are certainly other reasons to add the  attractiveness of online mba programs  also there are some disadvantages that  you should look into before taking these  programs hence let's delve into a few  pros and cons of an online mba program  first we will cover the pros of the  program the curriculum and faculty of  online programs can be compared to their  on-campus counterparts the very same  instructors teach the same curriculum as  on-campus courses hence the quality of  teaching and content delivery remains  consistent in online programs next one  is peer connectivity critiques of the  online program say that these programs  lose out on the on-campus experiences  such as face-to-face interactions with  professors and peers class debates and  placement fairs however most online  programs provided by reputed b schools  bridge their gap through meet your class  events career fairs one-to-one virtual  interactions and international projects  chat forums and online discussions  ensure that you have the advantages of  getting to know the global businesses  and business players through your  screens  the third benefit of an online mba is  that rote learning is not involved in it  most online courses have open books  tests and don't make students  learn by rote  furthermore these courses utilize  practical methods to test understanding  of business theory such as projects and  thorough assignments  another advantage of online mba is that  applicants who couldn't attend the  traditional full-time mba programs at  top-notch p-schools due to their high  tuition fees can participate in the  online courses of these schools for  lesser costs  also the students of an online mba  program continue to work which means  they don't lose out on their monthly  salary checks so there's definitely no  opportunity cost there's no relocation  and commuting costs no hostile and  stationary costs which means you will  end up saving a lot of time and money  on that note let's now understand a few  disadvantages of an online mba  although a few top online mba programs  have created interactive platforms and  chat rooms to overcome the communication  gap however they are not as effective as  on-campus experiences  you will miss out on the live class  experiences on on-campus events alumni  networking opportunities and  peer-to-peer camaraderie in addition to  that the career support provided by  online mba programs is yet to reach  efficiency as of its counterpart on  campus programs the next major demerit  of an online mba program is that they  don't qualify for student visa this  leads to trouble for students who want  to avail international post-study